<Layout title="Research" description="Research lines, active projects and publications of the HelioFísica y Clima Espacial USACH group.">

<section>
  <span class="section-title">Research</span>
  <h1>Research</h1>
  <p class="lead">Van Allen radiation belt physics, ULF waves, magnetospheric turbulence, and space weather prediction with machine learning.</p>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <span class="section-title">Research lines</span>

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1rem">
    <span class="badge badge-green">Space physics</span>
    <h3>Radiation belt dynamics</h3>
    <p>Mechanisms of energization, transport, and decay of relativistic electrons in the Van Allen belts. Enhancement and dropout events. Formation of ultrarelativistic remnant belts. Radial response to geomagnetic storms.</p>
    <p class="meta">Data: Van Allen Probes (MagEIS, REPT, EMFISIS, EFW), GOES, THEMIS</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1rem">
    <span class="badge badge-green">Space physics</span>
    <h3>ULF waves & magnetospheric turbulence</h3>
    <p>Role of electromagnetic ULF waves in trapped charged particle dynamics. Magnetospheric turbulence, total pressure balance, and wave-particle interactions.</p>
    <p class="meta">Data: Magnetometers (SAMBA, MACCS, THEMIS GBO, CARISMA), SuperDARN, THEMIS</p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="margin-bottom:1rem">
    <span class="badge badge-orange">Data science</span>
    <h3>Machine Learning for space weather</h3>
    <p>Prediction models for ground magnetic perturbations, geomagnetically induced currents (GIC), and empirical forecasting using deep learning (RNN, CNN, LSTM).</p>
    <p class="meta">Tools: Python, TensorFlow-Keras, PyTorch, Scikit-learn. Real-time OMNI data</p>
  </div>
</section>

